17c2151441aa4cd768d81aab1a497579ebb38ab05e18f83d5c" "q-105629/selection/3dff463cc384ac8627c411e00daa01d7743d43bb07d51607490aae23d412df65"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105629" :question/id #uuid "c3af26f3-6e90-5e80-9417-4c743f059326" :question/math-academy-id "q-105629" :question/problem "$$\nf(\\theta ,ϕ)=⟨\\text{_____},\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(\\theta ,ϕ)$ above parametrizes the sphere defined in Cartesian coordinates as ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=2.$ What is the first component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation generates a sphere of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at the origin.\nIn spherical polar coordinates, this sphere has the equation $\\rho =\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ.\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\theta ,ϕ) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $ϕ\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105629/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1e45977-275f-51ef-b8b5-f7a47c770ca5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105629"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105631/selection/9e0de166bffb11ce65ea51d2a21956d1b2a8ebc21023ba3b4953c4bf3039f24c" :answer/id #uuid "1c309398-04de-5ad1-886e-6a8d1988232d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105631/selection/b0f71af6299b45787db8e4b1e99c44fe4b81bb6574e8096ada9bfb35ee3b4b45" :answer/id #uuid "3365f326-f5c2-5dde-ab70-4e363ca8ca61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105631/selection/445f1734ca5c26e6ccaa49aa63addb6a1deed5f3a69a954d6a255435d8c89cde" :answer/id #uuid "1297dea6-c0dd-55dc-b64a-b2e449483ea4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105631/selection/f0e428f46dbbefd09cf292e52fa3f4d9bff195c74e5f48ec29525450a098cc7e" :answer/id #uuid "a1d65fea-f171-5213-af43-3edc50c9a84f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105631/selection/6ead3f28749c99cb198240e5f0fc847b17e3367fada98f0f39809ed5ef6454fa" :answer/id #uuid "a702befe-6a53-5908-97ea-b527847cf98c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105631/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c57a638b-5c42-5bf5-b5f9-174bfb424f03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105631/selection/445f1734ca5c26e6ccaa49aa63addb6a1deed5f3a69a954d6a255435d8c89cde" :answer-field/choices ["q-105631/selection/9e0de166bffb11ce65ea51d2a21956d1b2a8ebc21023ba3b4953c4bf3039f24c" "q-105631/selection/b0f7