e{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,5\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $ϕ\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $f$ is $5\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105617/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1e45977-275f-51ef-b8b5-f7a47c770ca5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105617"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105648/selection/ab4215ac33c23eaa2e3e8233470403f5c8def1f4530769192fee0ee30067d809" :answer/id #uuid "cc279c90-b3b7-539b-991b-b876baf4fee2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105648/selection/a1264653b3422c1758bb0348d5ce6698a82aead097802f2512a649a736ad0568" :answer/id #uuid "20db87c8-c0ad-510a-bb23-728ba771c0ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105648/selection/1d1f5e81c8a6c93fbc06c0fb37e43416ad9d32f3eded31de3e89584fed527d1e" :answer/id #uuid "6c7bec1b-aa2a-5775-916a-74a8792e5c5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105648/selection/31a789d99715028100e551ce7e44a491ad76ffd5be2699769e751a16e63938b4" :answer/id #uuid "4ca9e326-3cc1-5fd5-9e76-93e75fc3c0d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105648/selection/1cd75d1b01ec5ea72e6dd5706e0553c28c268c0d2b691504c0bd6b0c6ff94022" :answer/id #uuid "8c1373e1-1ad8-5fee-8534-82de5ad69c24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105648/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b10f350b-2ddb-56a8-8ad0-867a52eea511" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105648/selection/1cd75d1b01ec5ea72e6dd5706e0553c28c268c0d2b691504c0bd6b0c6ff94022" :answer-field/choices ["q-105648/selection/ab4215ac33c23eaa2e3e8233470403f5c8def1f4530769192fee0ee30067d809" "q-105648/selection/a1264653b3422c1758bb0348d5ce6698a82aead097802f2512a649a736ad0568" "q-105648/selection/1d1f5e81c8a6c93fbc06c0fb37e43416ad9d32f3eded31de3e89584fed527d1e" "q-105648/selection/31a789d99715028100e551ce7e44a491ad76ffd5be2699769e751a16e63938b4" "q-105648/selection/1cd75d1b01ec5ea72e6dd5706e0553c28c268c0d2b691504c0bd6b0c6ff94022"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105648" :question/id #uuid "90bae4d4-4f7e-5943-9a25-1065740ddf76" :question/math-academy-id "q-105648" :question/problem "$$\nf(\\theta ,ϕ)=⟨\\text{_____},\\,\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(\\theta ,ϕ)$ above parametrizes the sphere defined in Cartesian coordinates as ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}={\\pi }^{2}.$ What is the first component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "The given equation generates a sphere of radius $\\pi $ centered at the origin.\nIn spherical polar coordinates, this sphere has the equation $\\rho =\\pi .$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical polar coordinates of a point, then its Cartesian coordinates $(x,y,z)$ can be found using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ.\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\theta ,ϕ) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $ϕ\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105648/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f1e45977-275f-51ef-b8b5-f7a47c770ca5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105648"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105686/selection/4a18a8671dc91c86c3b75cab4669a74ca923ebf436e122bb1b0326e9330961c3" :answer/id #uuid "edc61c5a-283e-5131-bb9e-a0c2ba573d3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105686/selection/f56e5f57095b234d3d492054be1437b8fe93eee339b3c3316b32cae80befe394" :answer/id #uuid "c688b832-5aec-5f19-9ae1-e8a76d5d33b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105686/selection/2923a0294bcd54b613e37c0d65f5337179ccf95b58f93e5433a7e49b882d0200" :answer/id #uuid "8811ee64-af87-51e9-8e4e-c849160f01a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105686/selection/b6e7544faf9e09ebe11c362d103f8b9f4910bbe6f138cd6ff3fd72c8d08ce39c" :answer/id #uuid "22c31fe8-b54c-57bc-9bae-94d9d0652902" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105686/selection/200b1767dbbe95f9a61763781c435914613dc79cfd7630dd5d9bc8f72d8667a9" :answer/id #uuid "4cbbe258-c635-5700-8203-0a49951ddec9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105686/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "74d01d4b-6a8f-5295-8018-3a01f09bae90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105686/selection/f56e5f57095b234d3d492054be1437b8fe93eee339b3c3316b32cae80befe394" :answer-field/choices ["q-105686/selection/4a18a8671dc91c86c3b75cab4669a74ca923ebf436e122bb1b0326e9330961c3" "q-105686/selection/f56e5f57095b234d3d492054be1437b8fe93eee339b3c3316b32cae80befe394" "q-105686/selection/2923a0294bcd54b613e37c0d65f5337179ccf95b58f93e5433a7e49b882d0200" "q-105686/selection/b6e7544faf9e09ebe11c362d103f8b9f4910bbe6f138cd6ff3fd72c8d08ce39c" "q-105686/selection/200b1767dbbe95f9a61763781c435914613dc79cfd7630dd5d9bc8f72d8667a9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105686" :question/id #uuid "de032730-b4c9-509d-a255-b54cc05b2476" :question/math-academy-id "q-105686" :question/problem "$$\nf(\\theta ,ϕ)=⟨6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,\\text{_____},\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(\\theta ,ϕ)$ above parametrizes the ellipsoid defined in Cartesian coordinates as $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=1.$ What is the second component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following substitution:\n\n$$\nx=6X,\\,y=3Y,\\,z=4Z\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the Cartesian equation of our ellipsoid, we get\n\n$$\n{X}^{2}+{Y}^{2}+{Z}^{2}=1,\n$$\n\nwhich is the equation of a sphere of radius $1$ centered at the origin in $(X,Y,Z)$ coordinates.\nIn spherical polar coordinates, this sphere has the equation $\\rho =1.$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical polar coordinates of a point, then its $(X,Y,Z)$ coordinates can be found using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nX=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,Y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,Z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ.\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\theta ,ϕ) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6X,3Y,4Z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,3\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,4\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6\\cdot 1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,3\\cdot 1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,4\\cdot 1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $ϕ\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$\n\nTherefore, the second component of $f$ is $3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105686/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feb953f4-0a88-5d41-b62d-e8d7acd05801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105686"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105691/selection/0eaa891be64e6034d28d1e3706998aac4200db766b80d512df5d5e76acd43a7e" :answer/id #uuid "9cf901aa-e246-5be9-9c88-6a526f217fb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105691/selection/259784451e2d82e9b5376e5ca829cc4a67771487e3227805d458d65b5df92263" :answer/id #uuid "ee843141-7924-59b5-82d9-89b79f320015" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105691/selection/bfd909135dcfdcbffca7bc00cf3fd524184c596d295fb9b2ff71eca2da729085" :answer/id #uuid "bf17a6f7-aea2-511c-b189-df7e216609ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105691/selection/b396ec8e86d94aeeac9e6d3ee0a40b558bd5de9c5ce53a253ac21978f69eade5" :answer/id #uuid "e754928a-5bd7-5a6c-af64-9940fe0d1ecb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105691/selection/551541bc3fc83a5ac74c10fef9c02fb5a9ce8b99fbd1f0b5d92b2ba5edb614ab" :answer/id #uuid "1d780782-c04e-5d59-a9dd-22cd1f03ea4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105691/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9553b8a3-8d62-5e13-b72c-acc330ae1364" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105691/selection/551541bc3fc83a5ac74c10fef9c02fb5a9ce8b99fbd1f0b5d92b2ba5edb614ab" :answer-field/choices ["q-105691/selection/0eaa891be64e6034d28d1e3706998aac4200db766b80d512df5d5e76acd43a7e" "q-105691/selection/259784451e2d82e9b5376e5ca829cc4a67771487e3227805d458d65b5df92263" "q-105691/selection/bfd909135dcfdcbffca7bc00cf3fd524184c596d295fb9b2ff71eca2da729085" "q-105691/selection/b396ec8e86d94aeeac9e6d3ee0a40b558bd5de9c5ce53a253ac21978f69eade5" "q-105691/selection/551541bc3fc83a5ac74c10fef9c02fb5a9ce8b99fbd1f0b5d92b2ba5edb614ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105691" :question/id #uuid "95cac1d1-11d7-5a1b-b4e7-d28d5113fbb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-105691" :question/problem "$$\nf(\\theta ,ϕ)=⟨\\text{_____},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $f(\\theta ,ϕ)$ above parametrizes the ellipsoid defined in Cartesian coordinates as ${x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{9}=1.$ What is the first component of $f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we make the following substitution:\n\n$$\nx=X,\\,y=2Y,\\,z=3Z\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the Cartesian equation of our ellipsoid, we get\n\n$$\n{X}^{2}+{Y}^{2}+{Z}^{2}=1,\n$$\n\nwhich is the equation of a sphere of radius $1$ centered at the origin in $(X,Y,Z)$ coordinates.\nIn spherical polar coordinates, this sphere has the equation $\\rho =1.$\n\nIf $(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)$ are the spherical polar coordinates of a point, then its $(X,Y,Z)$ coordinates can be found using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nX=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,Y=\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,Z=\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ.\n$$\n\nNow, for any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\theta ,ϕ) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨X,2Y,3Z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,2\\rho \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,3\\rho \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,2\\cdot 1\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,3\\cdot 1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi )$ and $ϕ\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$\n\nTherefore, the first component of $f$ is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-105691/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feb953f4-0a88-5d41-b62d-e8d7acd05801"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105691"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-105662/selection/45c264210ac2725d1a1da817dfe29f2d46e675f2dde574f02b22fa40930d2b71" :answer/id #uuid "da028a19-6f55-58e2-a486-9db867350cb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105662/selection/a75ab5ac470af66ffe449befeab1d734f